## 4. Prohibited Uses and Abuse Prevention

The Licensee shall not use, modify, distribute, integrate, or otherwise operate the Software, in whole or in part, for any of the following purposes:

### 4.1 Malware and Malicious Software

- Creating, deploying, distributing, or operating malware, ransomware, spyware, trojans, worms, rootkits, or other malicious software.
- Unauthorized destruction, encryption, modification, or exfiltration of data.
- Unauthorized access to computer systems, networks, devices, or accounts.
- Circumventing security mechanisms for malicious or unauthorized purposes.
- Establishing unauthorized persistence, remote access, or command-and-control functionality.

### 4.2 Unauthorized Surveillance and Spying

- Secretly monitoring, recording, tracking, or surveilling individuals without appropriate authorization or lawful basis.
- Collecting private communications, credentials, personal information, or sensitive data without authorization.
- Deploying covert monitoring mechanisms, keyloggers, hidden recording functionality, or unauthorized tracking systems.
- Accessing cameras, microphones, location information, or other sensors without appropriate authorization and consent where required by law.
- Intercepting private communications or network traffic without appropriate authorization.

### 4.3 Covert and Unauthorized Operations

- Conducting unauthorized surveillance, intelligence collection, or reconnaissance against individuals, organizations, or computer systems.
- Concealing malicious functionality, unauthorized access, or unlawful activity.
- Deploying unauthorized backdoors, persistence mechanisms, or remote-control functionality.
- Using the Software to facilitate stalking, harassment, intimidation, extortion, or other unlawful conduct.
- Disguising malicious functionality as legitimate software functionality.

### 4.4 Illegal Activities

- Using the Software to facilitate criminal activity or intentional violations of applicable law.
- Circumventing legal restrictions or access controls for unlawful purposes.
- Facilitating fraud, identity theft, impersonation, or unauthorized financial activity.
- Assisting or enabling activities prohibited under applicable criminal or cybersecurity laws.
- Knowingly facilitating the unlawful acquisition, disclosure, or exploitation of protected information.

### 4.5 Circumvention of Security Safeguards

The Licensee shall not remove, disable, bypass, conceal, or circumvent security safeguards incorporated into the Software for the purpose of enabling activities prohibited by this License.

This provision does not prohibit legitimate modification, accessibility improvements, interoperability work, security testing, or authorized research.

### 4.6 Legitimate Security Research and Authorized Activities

Nothing in this section prohibits legitimate and authorized activities, including:

- Defensive cybersecurity research.
- Authorized penetration testing.
- Malware analysis in isolated research environments.
- Digital forensics and incident response.
- Security auditing and vulnerability assessment.
- Lawful system administration and monitoring.
- Educational research and controlled security experimentation.
- Authorized network analysis and diagnostics.

Such activities must be conducted with appropriate authorization and in compliance with applicable law.

### 4.7 Enforcement

Any use of the Software in violation of this section constitutes a material breach of this License and may result in termination of the rights granted under Section 14.

The Licensor reserves all rights and remedies available under applicable law.

